{% extends 'layouts/base.njk' %}
{% set pageType = 'Homepage' %}

{# Intro content #}
{% set introHeading = title %}
{% set introSummary %}
  {{ bannerSummary | safe }}
{% endset %}

{# Post and journal list content #}
{% set postListHeading = postsHeading %}
{% set postListSummary = postsSummary %}
{% set postListItems = collections.postFeed %}
{% set journalListHeading = journalHeading %}
{% set journalListSummary = journalSummary %}
{% set journalListItems = collections.journalFeed %}

{# Project list content #}
{% set projectListItems = collections.projects %}

{% block content %}
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    {% include "partials/components/intro.njk" %}

	<section class="[ now-list ] [ pad-bottom-400 ]">
		<div class="[ wrapper ] [ sf-flow ]">
			<h2 class="[ text-700 md:text-max ]">What am I up to?</h2>

			<div>
				<h3>Enjoying</h3>
				<p>I've recently moved back to my hometown Kirkby Lonsdale. Returning (a lot) older and wiser has given me a new appreciation of how beautiful it is around here. So I'm currently:</p>

				<ul>
					<li>Following a running traning plan</li>
					<li>Getting out walking</li>
					<li>Strength training to aid the running</li>
					<li>Trying out different places to work</li>
					<li>Starting to write a little more regularly</li>
					<li>Volunteering with local community groups and charities. So far I've helped out a local jumble sale and a community food center</li>
					<li>Speaking to a transformation coach on how I can help shift my mindset</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h3>Learning</h3>
				<p>Whilst I'm searching for my next role, I'm using the time to try and upskill in a few areas:</p>

				<ul>
					<li>Going through the <a href="https://www.totaltypescript.com/tutorials/beginners-typescript">Total TypeScript: Beginner's TypeScript course</a>. I've had experience with TypeScript in previous roles, but trying to improve my understanding and competency</li>
					<li>Using React to try and improve my understanding</li>
					<li>Doing some UI design practice work to improve Figma skills</li>
					<li>Getting more experince with headless content management systems. Currently using DatoCMS</li>
					<li><s>Trying to figure out the confusing world of Linkedin.</s> There are some nice communities and knowledge on there, but I was often feeling worse after visiting</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h3>Making</h3>
				<p>I've got a few bits I'm working on to keep myself in a routine and skills sharp whilst job hunting:</p>

				<ul>
					<li>Helping a friend out with a React/TypeScript/Dato project</li>
					<li>Designing a site as part of a skill swap arrangement. Once designed I will also be building the site</li>
					<li>Tinkering around with this site. I'm currently looking at little performance optimisations and considering whether to change my headless CMS</li>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h3>Reading</h3>
				<p>With a litte bit more free time, I'm trying to get into the habbit of putting some time aside to read regularly. So these books are currently on my side-table/list. They are a mixture of wellbeing, self-help and tech books.</p>

				<ul>
					<li><a href="https://accessibility-cookbook.com/">The Accessibility Cookbook</a> — Manuel Matuzović</li>
					<li><a href="https://abookapart.com/products/accessibility-for-everyone.html">Accessibility for Everyone</a> — Laura Kalbag</li>
					<li><a href="https://jamesclear.com/atomic-habits">Atomic Habits</a> — James Clear</li>
					<li><a href="https://www.waterstones.com/book/homecoming/john-bradshaw/9780749910549">Home Coming: Reclaiming and Championing Your Inner Child</a> — John Bradshaw</li>
					<li><a href="https://menshouldtalk.com/book/">The Expected Self</a> — Gareth Palmer (Men Should Talk)</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{% include "partials/components/article-list.njk" %}

	<section class="[ talks-list ] [ pad-top-400 pad-bottom-400 ]">
		<div class="[ wrapper ] [ sf-flow ]">
			<h2 class="[ talks-list__heading ][ text-700 md:text-max ]">Speaking and Writing</h2>
			<p class="section-intro">I am passionate about speaking and writing on a variety of topics. Particularly around accessibility, front-end development, performance and UI.</p>

			<ul class="pad-top-500" role="list">
				<li class="sf-flow">
					<h3><span>Accessibility and Content Creation</span></h3>
					<p>A short lightning talk at the June 2025 Champions of Accessibility Network (CAN) meetup. Based on my experinces at digitial agencies and trying to bridge the gap between product handover and external content teams in relation to accessibility awareness.</p>
				<a href="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1-0TK4OIRLYO_1fAlqcJkR6AY30ztNQ9EwUI6kDKPrOQ/edit?slide=id.p#slide=id.p" rel="noreferrer">View the Accessibility and Content Creation deck on Google Slides</a>
				</li>

				<li class="sf-flow">
					<h3><span>Testing Accessibility</span></h3>
					<p>A shared talk with Enik Jonas at a QA Beginners Club meetup around the importance of testing accessibility, alongside some tips and techniques. I also gave a version of this talk solo at <a href="https://www.meetup.com/mcrfred/events/288887240/?eventOrigin=group_events_list">McrFRED #81</a>.</p>
					<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cyGSVHi-J4A&t=1s" rel="noreferrer">View the Testing Accessibility talk on YouTube</a>
				</li>

				<li class="sf-flow">
					<h3><span>5 HTML elements, And a partridge in a despair tree</span></h3>
					<p>An article written for the 2022 HTMHell advent calendar. Spotlighting 5 HTML elements and how much you get for free with them compared to complex custom solutions.</p>
					<a href="https://www.htmhell.dev/adventcalendar/2022/16/">View the 5 HTML elements, And a partridge in a despair tree article on HTMHell</a>
				</li>

				<li class="sf-flow">
					<h3><span>Accessibility Champions: Trying to create an accessibility culture</span></h3>
					<p>A talk given at Manchester Tech Festival 2023. Using my accessibility champions journey at Code Computerlove.</p>
				</li>

				<li class="sf-flow">
					<h3><span>Start with the fundamentals</span></h3>
					<p>A talk given at a <a href="https://www.meetup.com/juniordeveloper-careers-manchester/events/299142969/?eventOrigin=group_past_events">Junior Developer Careers community meetup</a>. Highlighting the importance of learning the fundementals when starting a front end career, HTML, CSS and JavaScript.</p>
				</li>

				<li class="sf-flow">
					<h3><span>Culture leads to conformance<span></h3>
					<p>My first ever public talk for Human Centered Design (HCD) Manchester. Filled with nerves and learned so much since and from it.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	{% include "partials/components/activity-list.njk" %}
	{% include "partials/components/journal-list.njk" %}
    {% include "partials/components/project-list.njk" %}
  </main>
{% endblock %}
